# Unicode CLDR, locale ta, dateFields.json, field hour.
# A counted noun is CASE-MARKED in Tamil, not bare: the ago pattern is
# the DATIVE unit plus முன், and the in-N pattern is the LOCATIVE on
# the unit with no preposition at all.  Both case forms are unit
# surfaces in their own right, and both are CLDR's own wording.
# மணிநேரம் does not inflect for count in either direction -- CLDR gives
# the same wording for one hour and for N.  The everyday மணி is NOT a
# unit surface: its first dictionary sense is "bell", so it is read as
# an hour only beside a numeral, which the numeral fold does.
மணிநேரம்
